    "loader: AutoModelForImageTextToText -> SmolVLMForConditionalGeneration (transformers.models.smolvlm.modeling_smolvlm), transformers 5.23.0, torch 2.15.0, fp32 on cuda; attempts: ['AutoModelForImageTextToText: ok'].",
    "both towers have a clean FFN hook: vision SmolVLMVisionMLP.fc1/fc2 (GELU-tanh, bias) and text LlamaMLP.gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj (SwiGLU, no bias); we replace module.forward with a 32-lane block-skip forward and restore the original callable + weight tensors afterwards (verified: restore_max_abs_dlogit ~ 0).",
    "permutation applied physically to the weights (gate rows / up rows / down columns, fc1 rows+bias / fc2 columns) so the model is isomorphic and blocks are contiguous; only the reduction order inside down_proj changes, which is the fp32 floor.",
    "theta is the per-layer tau-quantile of per-token per-block L2 energies measured on 3 real calibration batches (V2/V4/V6 frames), so tau is the target fraction of skipped (token, block) pairs; energy_captured is the retained activation energy fraction and actual_skip is measured, not assumed.",
    "norm compensation: alpha = min(1.5, ||a||/||a_keep||) per token, computed from the same block energies (sqrt(E/E_keep)); mean_alpha reported per row.",
    "fidelity rows for tower='vision' report image-feature rel-L2 (post pixel-shuffle connector) as rel_l2; text/both report prefill logits at the last position. Both quantities are always present (rel_l2_feat / rel_l2_prefill_logit).",
    "generation is greedy, 24 new tokens, on a 2-frame V2 video (128 image tokens, seq_len 152); top1_agree/first_div/rouge_l compare against the dense generation.",
    "VQA uses a deterministic synthetic image (red square + green circle) and 4 hand-written yes/no + colour prompts; the dense model itself scores 1.00 accuracy and there are only 4 prompts, so vqa_acc is a coarse relative signal (it is not monotone in tau) and not an absolute capability claim.",
    "calibration transfer: actual_skip is measured on the evaluation forward and lands on ~tau for every tower (see rows), i.e. the per-layer theta quantiles taken from the 3 calibration frames transfer to unseen frames and prompts; energy_captured stays >= 0.989 at tau=0.6 because the dropped blocks carry little L2 energy.",
    "SPEED CAVEAT: the masking path still issues the dense GEMMs (PyTorch has no sparse FFN), so gpu timings for tau>0 are equal-or-worse than dense: the mask multiply plus the alpha rescale are pure overhead, e.g. at tau=0.6 vision 53.7 -> 56.8 ms, prefill 11.0 -> 14.1 ms, decode 8.2 -> 11.8 ms/token. The real saving is quantified separately in speed.ffn_op, where the FFN is recomputed with the kept columns sliced out (gate/up rows and down columns gathered) -- that is what a kernel would do.",
    "SPEED CAVEAT 2: per-token skipping cannot be expressed as one GEMM. ffn_op reports two sliced references: 'union' gathers every block any token needs (kept_block_frac, op_speedup) and saturates towards 1.0 as soon as tokens disagree -- it is a lower bound for batched dense kernels; 'single_mask' applies one median-token mask to the whole batch (single_mask_block_frac, op_speedup_single_mask) and is the best case a batched kernel can reach at this skip rate. Per-token kernels (the P1 CUDA/AVX-512 lanes) sit between the two.",
    "prefill logits are compared at the last position only; decode timings use a manual KV-cache loop (median of the timed steps after warm-up) and include the masking overhead of every text layer.",
